---
import AppLayout from '../../../../layouts/AppLayout.astro';
import { chatLikeGenZ, appPath, studio, supportLink } from '../../../../data/apps';

const path = appPath(chatLikeGenZ);
const deletionEmail = supportLink('Chat Like Gen Z account and data deletion');
---

<AppLayout
  title="Chat Like Gen Z Account and Data Deletion | AppCrazy Labs"
  description="Request deletion of a Chat Like Gen Z account and associated data without signing in. Find your Support ID, email the developer, and understand current deletion limits."
  canonicalPath={`${path}data-deletion/`}
  heading="Chat Like Gen Z data deletion"
  kicker="AppCrazy Labs · Privacy & support"
  deck="Request deletion of your account and associated data. No sign-in is needed to contact us."
  backLabel={chatLikeGenZ.name}
  backHref={path}
>
  <div slot="meta" class="hero-actions">
    <a class="button button-primary" href={deletionEmail}>Email a deletion request ↗</a>
    <a class="text-link" href={`${path}privacy/`}>Privacy policy →</a>
  </div>

  <p>
    <strong>Chat Like Gen Z is developed by Sidhanshu Udawat under the AppCrazy Labs brand.</strong>
    The Android test app creates an anonymous Firebase account for your conversion
    balance, even if you do not link Google. You can start a deletion request from
    this page without opening the app or signing in.
  </p>

  <section id="request" aria-labelledby="request-title">
    <h2 id="request-title">How to request deletion</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Email <a href={deletionEmail}>{studio.email}</a> with the subject
        “Chat Like Gen Z account and data deletion”. The button above opens a draft.
      </li>
      <li>
        Include your Support ID if you have it. In the current Android test build,
        find it at <strong>Settings → Save or recover balance</strong>, under
        “Support / test account ID”. If you linked Google, also tell us the email
        address used for that link, preferably by writing from that address.
      </li>
      <li>
        Say whether you want your app account and associated records deleted,
        specific support messages removed, or both. If you no longer have the
        Support ID, explain that in your email so we can discuss another way
        to locate and verify the account.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Do not send your password, payment-card number, purchase token, Firebase
      credential, private message text or identity documents. We may request
      limited additional information to confirm that the account belongs to you.
      We will reply with the status, any verification needed, what can be removed
      and any records that must be retained. No fixed completion time has been
      verified for the current test process.
    </p>
  </section>

  <aside class="note-callout" aria-label="Current deletion status">
    <strong>A request is not automatic deletion</strong>
    <p>
      The app has a Settings → Request account &amp; data deletion option in its
      managed-wallet test build. It opens an email draft, not an in-app account
      erasure operation. A complete support-side process for deleting the Firebase
      account and all associated server records has not yet been implemented and
      verified. We cannot promise that sending the request immediately removes them.
    </p>
  </aside>

  <section aria-labelledby="records-title">
    <h2 id="records-title">What the request needs to cover</h2>
    <p>
      The records associated with a Support ID can include the Firebase
      Authentication account, wallet balance, conversion-operation records
      (including generated results), credit grants, billing-account mappings,
      reward tickets and related verification records. If you linked Google,
      the Firebase account can also include your Google account identifier,
      email and basic profile. Support emails and attachments you sent us
      are a separate category.
    </p>
    <p>
      We will review those categories when responding, but the current backend
      has no verified complete account-deletion workflow. Deleting only the
      Firebase sign-in account would leave associated Firestore records behind.
      Until a verified process is in place, we cannot claim that every category
      will be erased on request. See the <a href={`${path}privacy/#retention`}>retention section of the privacy policy</a>
      {' '}for the current storage status.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="device-title">
    <h2 id="device-title">Data on your device</h2>
    <p>
      Android’s clear-storage control or uninstalling the app removes its local
      writing profile, pending conversion and recent result from that device.
      Copies you sent to other apps, screenshots and device backups may remain
      until you remove them there. Clearing local data does not delete the
      Firebase account, remote wallet or conversion records. An unlinked guest
      account may then be difficult to identify, so save your Support ID first
      if you plan to request server-data deletion.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="retention-title">
    <h2 id="retention-title">Records that may need to remain</h2>
    <p>
      Some purchase and credit records may need to be retained for transaction
      integrity, fraud prevention, accounting, disputes or legal obligations.
      The current app is limited to internal test purchases; Google Play controls
      its own transaction and payment history, which a request to us cannot erase.
      Google also controls data processed by AdMob and Gemini under its own policies.
    </p>
    <p>
      No verified retention period or complete exception schedule exists yet for
      the app’s server records. Conversion records have a seven-day deletion marker,
      but Firestore automatic deletion is not enabled, so that marker is not a
      seven-day deletion promise. If a record must remain after a request, we will
      explain the reason and the applicable duration or criteria when known.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="contact-title">
    <h2 id="contact-title">Contact</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>App:</strong> Chat Like Gen Z<br />
      <strong>Legal developer / publisher:</strong> Sidhanshu Udawat<br />
      <strong>Privacy contact:</strong> Sidhanshu Udawat - <a href={deletionEmail}>{studio.email}</a>
    </p>
    <p>Last updated: <time datetime="2026-10-06">6 October 2026</time>.</p>
  </section>
</AppLayout>
